Repair the complete source below and return a corrected complete `Solution.java`. The API `public static String collapseDuplicates(String text)` must split input on one or more Java whitespace characters, discard leading and trailing whitespace, collapse each run of adjacent exactly equal case-sensitive tokens to one token, and join retained tokens with one ASCII space. Empty or whitespace-only input returns `""`; null throws `IllegalArgumentException`. Nonadjacent duplicates remain, input is not mutated, and punctuation is part of a token. The known-bad implementation incorrectly merges tokens that differ only by case.

```java
public final class Solution {
    private Solution() {}

    public static String collapseDuplicates(String text) {
        if (text == null) throw new IllegalArgumentException("null text");
        String trimmed = text.trim();
        if (trimmed.isEmpty()) return "";
        String[] tokens = trimmed.split("\\s+");
        StringBuilder out = new StringBuilder(tokens[0]);
        for (int i = 1; i < tokens.length; i++) {
            if (!tokens[i].equalsIgnoreCase(tokens[i - 1])) {
                out.append(' ').append(tokens[i]);
            }
        }
        return out.toString();
    }
}
```

